s_rule_855cbba0_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For $f(x) = x^2$ and $g(x) = x$, which derivative quotient appears when applying L'Hôpital's rule to $\\lim_{x\\to 0}f(x)/g(x)$?","options":["$\\dfrac{x^2}{x}$","$\\dfrac{2x}{1}$","$\\dfrac{1}{2x}$","$\\dfrac{x}{x^2}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c7a65cd2a475f4c37aa0c1bc","time_limit":25,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_lhopitals_rule_855cbba0_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which limit is explicitly an example that can be evaluated using L'Hôpital's rule?","options":["$\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\frac{\\ln x}{x}$","$\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sin x}{x}$ as a justification of its own value","$\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to 0}(x+1)$","$\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to 1}x^2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b49fa09438e81b9ee6fff662","time_limit":20,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_lhopitals_rule_855cbba0_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which assumption is required about the denominator derivative in L'Hôpital's rule?","options":["$g'$ is nonzero on $I\\setminus\\{x_0\\}$","$g'$ is zero on $I\\setminus\\{x_0\\}$","$g$ is constant on $I\\setminus\\{x_0\\}$","$g$ must be positive on all of $I$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0a8c699be9b1a7f0eddb8162","time_limit":30,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_lhopitals_rule_855cbba0_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"In the statement of L'Hôpital's rule, what may the value $L$ be?","options":["Only a positive real number","Only $0$","Only a finite nonzero real number","An element of $[-\\infty,+\\infty]$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0fd7124786cafcc75fa3b897","time_limit":30,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_lhopitals_rule_855cbba0_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f,g$ be differentiable near $x_0$, with $g$ and $g'$ nonzero for $x\\ne x_0$. Suppose $f(x),g(x)\\to0$ and $\\lim_{x\\to x_0} f'(x)/g'(x)=5$. What does L'Hôpital's rule imply about $\\lim_{x\\to x_0}f(x)/g(x)$?","options":["$\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to x_0}\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} = 5$","$\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to x_0}\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} = 0$","$\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to x_0}f(x) = 5$","$\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to x_0}g(x) = 5$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"611dc537c5e637414b55e0d1","time_limit":30,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_lhopitals_rule_855cbba0_009","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why is it circular to use L'Hôpital's rule to justify $\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sin x}{x} = 1$?","options":["Because the quotient is not of type $0/0$","Because $x$ is not differentiable near $0$","Because the derivative of $\\sin x$ depends on that limit","Because L'Hôpital's rule never applies at finite points"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d6c7720baa0ed94cfeaf534d","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_lhopitals_rule_855cbba0_010","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which statement best describes the non-circularity requirement in l'Hôpital's rule?","options":["The existence of $f'$ and $g'$ must not rely on 